---
/**
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SEEING.MD HOME PAGE
 * Route: /
 * Type: Page
 * Page version: 1.5.0 (Show it working; SEEING.md version read from the file)
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * PURPOSE
 * Introduces SEEING.md as a portable perception specification for people and
 * AI. One question carries the page: what have we already defined?
 *
 * AUDIENCE AND PRIMARY ACTION
 * - Audience: Leaders, teams, AI practitioners, designers, developers,
 *   consultants, coaches, and individual practitioners
 * - Primary action: Download SEEING.md
 * - Leader action: Seeing First, linked to its section on seedifferent.xyz
 *
 * EXPERIENCE / STRUCTURE
 * The black hero establishes the inherited definition; the white middle
 * offers two ways of looking again; the black close gives one clear action.
 * Hero (what it is) → AI scales what we see, with one exchange → Get the
 * file and use it → Seeing First → Footer.
 * The composition shifts between broad and reading measures instead of
 * repeating the same narrow left-aligned column.
 *
 * COMPOSITIONAL PASS (15 October 2026)
 * Retained the original copy and Suede tokens, but composed the middle
 * with contrasting asymmetric relationships, changed the closing headline
 * to "Seeing comes first," moved limits under the download instructions,
 * and moved the secondary Seeing First invitation to the footer.
 * No additional cards, images, sections, or design languages.
 *
 * TYPOGRAPHY / RHYTHM PASS (17 October 2026)
 * Preserves the editorial composition and copy while clarifying heading
 * hierarchy, easing display tracking, and tightening connected spacing.
 * Gives the AI explanation a more comfortable reading column.
 *
 * HEADLINE SCALE PASS (17 October 2026)
 * A 60px hero and one shared 48px section-heading scale preserve a clear
 * hierarchy; the supporting assumptions heading uses a quieter 36px scale.
 * Responsive hero sizing remains continuous across the mobile breakpoint.
 *
 * SUEDE HERO PASS (18 October 2026)
 * Hero recomposed after Brian Gardner's Suede homepage: no eyebrow, a
 * larger display headline set in the left half of a two-column grid, one
 * quiet supporting line, and paired buttons (filled download, outlined
 * "How to use it"). The right column is intentionally empty for now.
 * Header link becomes an outlined uppercase label, as in Suede's nav.
 *
 * SUEDE TYPE-SCALE PASS (18 October 2026)
 * Matched Suede's theme.json: font loaded without the optical-size axis
 * (Suede's file has wdth/wght/slnt only), hero headline 48-60px at line
 * height 1.0, supporting line 18px, buttons and header link 12px, site
 * name 16px (kept mixed case so .md stays lowercase), body tracking 0.01em.
 *
 * SUEDE ALIGNMENT PASS (18 October 2026)
 * Headings at line height 1.0; other line heights on Suede's ladder
 * (1, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75). Body stays 18px on phones. Buttons carry no
 * arrows and centre their label. Link underlines 1px at 2px offset.
 * Section spacing uses Suede's fluid spacing presets; no 120px.
 *
 * SUBTRACTION PASS (18 October 2026)
 * Asked of each section what it repeats. Removed: numbered eyebrows,
 * the "Who got this wrong?" block (it lives in the file), the two limits
 * blocks (now one line under the download), the closing "Seeing is the
 * first decision." line, the header download link (now Seeing First),
 * and the rule between the two white sections. Revised: the premise
 * question is now the second section's heading; the download section's
 * heading is "Get the file."
 *
 * FLOW BAND AND READING PASS (18 October 2026)
 * Header button removed. Notice → Question → See again → Act moves into
 * its own black band, centred, between the two white sections. Both white
 * sections now read top to bottom in one column: heading, then body at
 * the 640px measure in 80% black. Seeing First becomes its own section
 * above the footer with a statement and a filled button.
 *
 * HERO SPACING (18 October 2026)
 * Hero no longer fills the viewport; its height is its content plus the
 * header (80px) and the 100px spacing preset above and below.
 *
 * QUESTION SECTION HEADING (18 October 2026)
 * Heading shortened to "The smallest change."; the full premise question
 * now opens the section's paragraph, keeping it near the top of the page.
 *
 * HERO FIGURE (18 October 2026)
 * The empty right column now holds a line drawing from the "standing in"
 * image: a figure (60% white) standing inside an amber ring, the viewpoint
 * it occupies. Decorative only; hidden below 1000px.
 *
 * FRAMED HERO FIGURE (18 October 2026)
 * The figure sits on a barely lifted panel inside four 1px amber corner
 * brackets offset 20px outside it, as on Suede's homepage. Its line is set
 * beneath as a caption, with "dropping" as the one amber word. Strokes
 * thinned to 3 to sit closer to the 1px frame.
 *
 * SHOW-IT-WORKING PASS (31 October 2026)
 * The page described SEEING.md but never showed it working, and the AI
 * connection waited until the third section. Now: the hero says what the
 * file is and who it's for (caption removed from the figure); the second
 * section carries "AI scales what we see", the smallest-change question,
 * and one exchange from examples/employment-gap.md; using it is one step
 * (copy button, where to put it in Claude, ChatGPT and coding tools); the
 * close offers Seeing First plus two quiet doors (what did your AI ask
 * you, new versions). Removed: the flow band and the separate smallest-
 * change section, both now carried by the example. Added a sharing image
 * (/og.png). Version and instruction are read from SEEING.md.
 *
 * CAPTION AND RESEARCH PASS (31 October 2026)
 * Amber corner brackets removed from the hero figure; the figure gains a
 * caption that ties it to what SEEING.md is ("Your AI starts from where
 * you're standing."). The AI section gains one research line before the
 * example: over half of managers who use AI have used it on a decision
 * about a person, and most were never trained in what to look for
 * (Resume Builder 2025, DLPA 2026), which sets up the employment-gap case.
 *
 * LEADERSHIP EXAMPLE (31 October 2026)
 * The homepage example is now org change (examples/org-change.md):
 * "resistance" as the unexamined word. The research line is broadened to
 * "decisions about their people" so it introduces change as well as
 * hiring. How It Works now carries the engagement example instead of the
 * near-duplicate "persuade my team to accept this change".
 *
 * BUTCHER HERO (31 October 2026)
 * After a Jack Butcher-style pass: the mechanism, drawn. One ring with a
 * gap (the blind spot, in amber), an arrow, and the same ring repeated
 * nine times. Caption: "AI doesn't add blind spots. It copies yours."
 *
 * GARDNER PASS (31 October 2026)
 * Subtraction and precision on the Butcher hero: the panel is removed so
 * the drawing sits on black; one stroke width throughout and a wider
 * amber gap so the repeated blind spot reads at a glance; the caption is
 * left-aligned at the hero's supporting size and in its quietest colour;
 * the drawing now shows on phones, below the button, instead of hiding;
 * the sharing image (/og.png) carries the same drawing.
 *
 * SUEDE ALIGNMENT (31 October 2026)
 * Checked against Suede's DESIGN.md. Outline buttons fill with gold on
 * hover; on black, buttons keep white text (gold as a mark). Widths use
 * 640 / 960 / 1280 only. Type sizes on the scale (24px, not 22px). The
 * expanded width on "Get the file." is removed. Hero phone padding comes
 * from the spacing scale; compact gaps use 10 and 16px; line heights stay
 * on the 1 / 1.25 / 1.5 / 1.75 ladder.
 *
 * DEPENDENCIES
 * - Layout: Standalone Astro page; no shared layout dependency
 * - Assets: Embedded open-frame SVG logo/favicon and public /SEEING.md
 * - Services: Google Fonts, Fathom, Cabin, and SEE DIFFERENT
 * - Hosting: Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets
 *
 * EDITING GUARDRAILS
 * - Suede: Google Sans Flex; type scale 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24, 30, 36, 48,
 *   60px (hero display may exceed 60px); body 18px / 1.75; headings 500.
 * - Spacing scale: 20, 30, 40, 60, 80, 100px. Reading measure 640px;
 *   composition width 1280px.
 * - Color: black, white, and #aa6600 only, through the opacity ladder
 *   (80 / 60 / 50 / 15). Primary buttons are accent-filled.
 * - Width axis: standard width throughout; expanded and condensed widths are
 *   not used until a statement needs one deliberately.
 * - Motion: 250ms interface transitions, ease-out.
 * - Before adding a section, ask what it repeats. Keep one method on the page.
 * - Keep the downloadable specification synchronized with the canonical
 *   SEEING.md file at the repository root.
 * - Do not imply that SEEING.md resolves every category of AI safety risk.
 * - Keep external links secure with rel="noopener".
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

const specification = readFileSync(new URL('../../SEEING.md', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
const release = specification.match(/\*\*Version (.+?)\*\*/)?.[1];
const conversationPrompt = specification.match(/Then tell the AI:\n\n> (.+)/)?.[1]?.replaceAll('`', '');
if (!release || !conversationPrompt) throw new Error('Check SEEING.md version and activation language before publishing the homepage.');

const title = 'SEEING.md — The Perception Behind Intent';
const description =
  'A free file you give your AI, so it questions the definition before it builds on it. For leaders and teams who do real work with AI.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://seeing.md/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://seeing.md/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="We don't question what we've already defined. A figure standing inside an amber ring. SEEING.md." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://seeing.md/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%2032%2032%22%3E%3Cstyle%3Epath%7Bstroke%3A%2311110f%7D%40media%28prefers-color-scheme%3Adark%29%7Bpath%7Bstroke%3A%23fff%7D%7D%3C%2Fstyle%3E%3Cpath%20d%3D%22M20%204H4V28H28V10%22%20fill%3D%22none%22%20stroke-width%3D%223.2%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Google+Sans+Flex:wdth,wght@75..125,100..1000&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <script src="https://scripts.withcabin.com/hello.js" async defer></script>
    <!-- Fathom - beautiful, simple website analytics -->
    <script src="https://cdn.usefathom.com/script.js" data-site="MWASYWBA" defer></script>
    <!-- / Fathom -->
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="wrap header-inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="SEEING.md home">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="24" height="24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M20 4H4V28H28V10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.2" />
          </svg>
          <span>SEEING.md</span>
        </a>
        <a class="button header-guide" href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero dark" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="wrap hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <h1 id="hero-title">We don’t question what we’ve already defined.</h1>
            <p class="names">SEEING.md is a free file you give your AI, so it questions the definition before it builds on it.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button" href="/SEEING.md" download onclick="window.fathom?.trackEvent('SEEING.md download');">Download SEEING.md</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figure class="hero-space">
            <svg class="hero-figure" viewBox="14 48 342 144" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M103.8 116.2 A44 44 0 1 1 63.8 76.2" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M63.8 76.2 A44 44 0 0 1 103.8 116.2" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M130 120 H184 M172 108 L184 120 L172 132" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M247.9 66.4 A18 18 0 1 1 231.6 50.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M231.6 50.1 A18 18 0 0 1 247.9 66.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M299.9 66.4 A18 18 0 1 1 283.6 50.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M283.6 50.1 A18 18 0 0 1 299.9 66.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M351.9 66.4 A18 18 0 1 1 335.6 50.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M335.6 50.1 A18 18 0 0 1 351.9 66.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M247.9 118.4 A18 18 0 1 1 231.6 102.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M231.6 102.1 A18 18 0 0 1 247.9 118.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M299.9 118.4 A18 18 0 1 1 283.6 102.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M283.6 102.1 A18 18 0 0 1 299.9 118.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M351.9 118.4 A18 18 0 1 1 335.6 102.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M335.6 102.1 A18 18 0 0 1 351.9 118.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M247.9 170.4 A18 18 0 1 1 231.6 154.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M231.6 154.1 A18 18 0 0 1 247.9 170.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M299.9 170.4 A18 18 0 1 1 283.6 154.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M283.6 154.1 A18 18 0 0 1 299.9 170.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M351.9 170.4 A18 18 0 1 1 335.6 154.1" stroke="var(--w60)" stroke-width="3" /><path d="M335.6 154.1 A18 18 0 0 1 351.9 170.4" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="3" /></svg>
            <figcaption>AI doesn’t add blind spots. It copies yours.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ai" id="why" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="statement">
            <h2 id="ai-title">AI scales what we see.<span>And what we don’t.</span></h2>
            <p>What if the smallest change with the greatest consequence isn’t a change in what we do, but a change in how we see? Before we hand a task to AI, we have already given it a way of seeing the situation. A more rigorous answer can still begin with an unexamined question.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence">
            <p class="stat">More than half of managers who use AI have used it on decisions about their people. Most were never shown what to look for.</p>
            <p class="aside">Resume Builder survey of 1,342 US managers, 2025. DLPA survey of 1,008 Australians, 2026.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="exchange" aria-label="An example">
            <div class="turn">
              <p class="who">You ask</p>
              <p class="said">Write a plan to overcome resistance to the reorganisation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="turn with">
              <p class="who">With SEEING.md, the AI asks first</p>
              <p class="said">You’ve described the team’s response as resistance. Do you know what they’re objecting to? Some of it may be information about the plan rather than something to overcome.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="shift">It didn’t refuse or take sides. It made the hidden decision visible, and left the choice with you.</p>
            <p class="aside">Illustrative response, condensed. <a href="/how-it-works/#an-example">See another example</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="use dark" id="use" aria-labelledby="use-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="use-grid">
            <div class="use-primary">
              <h2 id="use-title">Get the file.</h2>
              <p class="intro">A portable file for examining what shapes intent before AI amplifies it.</p>
              <a class="button" href="/SEEING.md" download onclick="window.fathom?.trackEvent('SEEING.md download');">Download SEEING.md</a>
              <p class="note">Version {release} · Free under CC BY 4.0</p>
              <p class="note">A lens, not the lens: question this file too. It addresses the human assumptions behind AI use; it does not prevent misuse, deception, or loss of control.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="use-guide">
              <h3>Use it in your work</h3>
              <p>Attach it to an AI conversation, a brief, or a project. Then ask the AI to read it first.</p>
              <blockquote id="conversation-prompt">{conversationPrompt}</blockquote>
              <button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy="conversation-prompt" hidden>Copy instruction</button>
              <p id="copy-status" class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
              <h4>Where to put it</h4>
              <dl class="places">
                <div><dt>Claude</dt><dd>Add the file to a Project, and the instruction to the project’s instructions.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>ChatGPT</dt><dd>Attach it to the conversation, or add it to a Project’s files.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Coding tools</dt><dd>Keep it in the repository and point to it from CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md.</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="seeing-first" id="seeing-first" aria-label="Seeing First">
        <div class="wrap seeing-first-inner">
          <p>Your AI asked the question. Seeing First helps your team ask it.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://seedifferent.xyz/#seeing-first" rel="noopener">Seeing First</a>
        </div>
        <div class="wrap doors">
          <p>What did your AI ask you? <a href="mailto:hello@seeing.md?subject=What%20my%20AI%20asked">Tell us at hello@seeing.md</a>. To hear about new versions, <a href="mailto:hello@seeing.md?subject=New%20versions">write with “New versions”</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="origin">SEEING.md grew from <a href="https://seedifferent.xyz/#book" rel="noopener"><em>The Perception Miracle</em></a> and more than 500 explorations. Its form was influenced by Brian Gardner’s DESIGN.md.</p>
        <div class="footer-meta">
          <span>© 2026 <a href="https://billfox.co/" rel="author">Bill Fox</a>. Licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>.</span>
          <a href="mailto:hello@seeing.md">hello@seeing.md</a>
          <a href="https://seedifferent.xyz" rel="noopener">SEE DIFFERENT</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/billfoxco/seeing-md" rel="noopener">Source and changelog</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        const status = document.getElementById('copy-status');
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
          const source = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy);
          if (!source || !navigator.clipboard) return;
          button.hidden = false;
          button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
            try {
              await navigator.clipboard.writeText(source.textContent.trim());
              status.textContent = 'Instruction copied.';
              window.fathom?.trackEvent('SEEING.md instruction copied');
            } catch {
              const range = document.createRange(); range.selectNodeContents(source);
              const selection = getSelection(); selection.removeAllRanges(); selection.addRange(range);
              status.textContent = 'Selected. Press Ctrl+C or Cmd+C to copy.';
            }
          });
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --ink: #000; --paper: #fff; --amber: #aa6600;
    --w80: rgba(255,255,255,.8); --w60: rgba(255,255,255,.6); --w15: rgba(255,255,255,.15);
    --b80: rgba(0,0,0,.8); --b60: rgba(0,0,0,.6); --b50: rgba(0,0,0,.5); --b15: rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    --section-heading: clamp(36px, 3.8vw, 48px);
    --support-heading: clamp(30px, 3vw, 36px);
    --content: 1280px; --measure: 640px;
    --gutter: clamp(20px, 4vw, 80px);
    /* Suede spacing presets */
    --space-30: clamp(20px, 3vw, 30px); --space-40: clamp(30px, 4vw, 40px);
    --space-60: clamp(40px, 6vw, 60px); --space-80: clamp(60px, 8vw, 80px);
    --space-100: clamp(70px, 10vw, 100px);
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Google Sans Flex", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; letter-spacing: .01em;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
  }
  h1, h2, h3, p, blockquote { margin: 0; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0; }
  h1, h2, h3 { text-wrap: balance; }
  p { text-wrap: pretty; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .wrap { width: 100%; max-width: var(--content); margin-inline: auto; }
  .site-header, main > section, footer { padding-inline: var(--gutter); }
  .dark { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 10px;
    padding: 20px 30px; background: var(--amber); color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--amber); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 250ms ease-out, color 250ms ease-out, border-color 250ms ease-out;
  }
  .button:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--amber); }
  /* On black, gold stays a mark: the hover keeps white text inside the gold border. */
  .dark .button:hover { color: var(--paper); }
  :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--amber); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .dark :focus-visible { outline-color: var(--paper); }

  .site-header { position: absolute; inset: 0 0 auto; z-index: 1; padding-block: var(--space-30); color: var(--paper); }
  .header-inner { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-30); }
  .wordmark { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: .01em; text-decoration: none; }
  .wordmark svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; }
  .wordmark svg { display: block; flex: 0 0 20px; }
  .header-guide { background: transparent; border-color: var(--amber); padding: 14px 20px; min-height: 44px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .header-guide:hover { background: var(--amber); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--amber); }

  .hero { padding-block: calc(80px + var(--space-100)) var(--space-100); }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, .85fr); gap: var(--space-80); align-items: center; }
  .hero h1 { max-width: var(--measure); font-size: clamp(48px, 4.2vw, 60px); line-height: 1; }
  .hero .names { max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-30); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--w60); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; margin-top: var(--space-40); }
  /* Figure on a barely lifted panel, with its caption */
  /* The drawing sits directly on black: no panel, caption set like Suede's. */
  .hero-space { margin: 0 0 0 auto; width: 100%; max-width: 380px; }
  .hero-figure { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .hero-space figcaption { max-width: 360px; margin-top: var(--space-40); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--w60); text-wrap: balance; }

  /* White reading sections: heading, then body, one column */
  .ai { padding-block: var(--space-100); }
  .statement h2 { max-width: 960px; font-size: var(--section-heading); line-height: 1; }
  .statement h2 span { display: block; }
  .statement p { max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-30); font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--b80); }


